<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Waterberg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1904</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Battle of Hamakari · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herero-wars">Herero Wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Waterberg was fought on 11 August 1904 at the Waterberg plateau in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-south-west-africa">German South West Africa</a>, now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/namibia">Namibia</a>, between German troops under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lothar-von-trotha">Lothar von Trotha</a> and the Herero. The Herero broke out to the east, where many thousands died in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/omaheke">Omaheke</a> desert, which the Germans sealed off. It marked the start of the Herero and Nama <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genocide">genocide</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-waterberg.jpg" alt="Battle of Waterberg" width="320" height="185" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:General_von_Trotha_and_his_staff_at_Hamakari,_1904.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
